  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pr&#xE9;vention et r&#xE9;ponses aux VBG/AES et offre de soins vitaux en Sant&#xE9; de la Reproduction aux populations affect&#xE9;es des districts Antalaha, Vohemar, Sambava apr&#xE8;s le passage du cyclone GAMANE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the project is to prevent and respond to Gender-Based Violence and provide vital reproductive health care to affected populations in the districts of Antalaha, Vohemar, and Sambava following the passage of Cyclone Gamane. UNFPA and partners support the upgrading of local authority and humanitarian actor capabilities, updates health providers, supports multisectoral GBV management, educates communities on sexual abuse and sexual exploitation, provides Sexual Reproductive Health and Dignity Kits to facilities, deploy midwives, managing obstetric complications and refreshing emergency health systems. A total of 18,566 people, including 8,054 women, 1,226 men, 9,286 children, and 892 persons with disabilities, directly benefit from these interventions.</narrative>
  </description>
